-- title:
--   Full right Λ-sublattices of locally principal ideals remain locally principal
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and a prime number $q'$, and suppose $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $q'$ in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87), i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the base change $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element is a unit) precisely when $q'$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ that is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among submodules with these properties. For a unit $g$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, write $\Lambda(g)$ for [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19), the set of $z$ in the algebra whose image $z\otimes 1$ lies in $g$ times the additive subgroup generated by the tensors $\lambda\otimes\alpha$ with $\lambda\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adèle. Given such a unit $y$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $K\le\Lambda(y)$ with $K\Lambda\subseteq K$ and with $n\cdot\Lambda(y)\subseteq K$ for some nonzero natural number $n$, the conclusion is that $K=\Lambda(x)$ for some unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$.
--
--   This is the local principality of right $\Lambda$-ideals in a definite quaternion algebra ramified at a single prime, in the adelic form: a finite-index right $\Lambda$-submodule of a locally principal right ideal $\mathbb{H}\cap y\widehat{\Lambda}$ is again of the shape $\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}$. It is obtained from the case $y=1$ ([`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_ofFiniteIdele_eq_of_forall_mul_mem`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_ofFiniteIdele_eq_of_forall_mul_mem)) together with the behaviour of [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) under multiplication by diagonal idèles, and it is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development to identify kernel ideals of isogenies of supersingular curves and to count subideals in Hecke sets.
-- source:
